The reference shows a chair seen from above, with armrests and a seat. In the drawing, the chairs are the three at the top, near y=155, at x≈67, 237 and 408.

The three partial chairs at the very top (y≈10) are cut off by the edge of the drawing. They are the backs of chairs from a row above, so I am counting them as partial instances. Their centers sit near y=10 and the visible portion is small. Since the reference shows a full chair, I'm including only the three complete ones to avoid inventing instances.

